NOTICE OF MEASURE TO BE VOTED ON;
NOTICE OF LAST DAY TO FILE ARGUMENTS;
NOTICE OF LAST DAY TO FILE REBUTTAL ARGUMENTS
NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the following measure is to be voted on by qualified voters
residing within Upland Unified School District the General Election to be held on Tuesday,
November 3, 2026.
Measure “_”
“To improve the quality of education by modernizing, constructing, upgrading and
equipping classrooms, restrooms/school facilities, career technical classrooms/labs; replace
roofs; make safety/security improvements; and renovate/replace electrical/plumbing/sewer
systems; shall Upland Unified School District’s measure be adopted, authorizing $236,700,000
of bonds at legal rates, levying approximately $47.50 per $100,000 assessed value (raising
$14,200,000 annually) while bonds are outstanding, with audits, independent oversight, NO
money for salaries, including administrators, only Upland USD educational facilities?”
BONDS YES
BONDS NO
NOTICE IS FURTHER GIVEN that this measure will pass only if approved by 55% of the
district’s registered voters who vote in this election.
NOTICE IS FURTHER GIVEN that noon on August 17, 2026, is the last day and hour that
arguments for or against the measure may be filed by mail, email, fax or in person with the San
Bernardino County Registrar of Voters. Arguments shall not exceed 300 words in length and
shall be accompanied by the statement set forth in Section 9600 of the Elections Code.
Additional information regarding the submission of arguments may be obtained from the San
Bernardino County Registrar of Voters.
NOTICE IS ALSO HEREBY GIVEN that 5 p.m. on August 21, 2026, is the last day and hour
that rebuttals to the arguments for or against the measure may be filed by mail, email, fax or in
person with the San Bernardino County Registrar of Voters. Rebuttals shall not exceed 250
words in length and shall be accompanied by the statement set forth in Section 9600 of the
Elections Code. Additional information regarding the submission of rebuttals may be obtained
from the San Bernardino County Registrar of Voters.
